<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS - Australia merchandise imports rise in Oct.</title>
<headline>RTRS - Australia merchandise imports rise in Oct.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian merchandise imports rose one percent in October to A$6.323 billion seasonally adjusted from A$6.242 billion in September, the Australian Bureau of Statistics said.</p>
<p>This compares with seasonally adjusted imports of A$6.078 billion in October 1995.</p>
<p>In unadjusted terms, merchandise imports rose 12 percent to A$7.170 billion in October from A$6.389 billion in September and compared to A$6.701 billion in October 1995.</p>
<p>Economists had on average forecast a rise of around 0.5 percent in seasonally adjusted imports for October.  </p>
<p>    SEASONALLY ADJ	   Oct 96    Sept 96	 Oct 95</p>
<p>    Merchandise imports  6.323 bln   6.242 bln   6.078 bln</p>
<p>    Consumption goods    1.708 bln   1.728 bln   1.570 bln</p>
<p>    Capital goods	  1.400 bln   1.507 bln   1.452 bln</p>
<p>    Intermediate goods   3.215 bln   3.007 bln   3.056 bln</p>
<p>UNADJUSTED</p>
<p>    Merchandise imports  7.170 bln   6.389 bln   6.701 bln</p>
<p>    Consumption goods    2.080 bln   1.800 bln   1.857 bln</p>
<p>    Capital goods	  1.596 bln   1.563 bln   1.616 bln</p>
<p>    Intermediate goods   3.494 bln   3.026 bln   3.228 bln</p>
